{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows propranolol hydrochloride injection from Fresenius Kabi and Hikma as Current since 2023-10-31; our 40 mg tablets trace to Bryant Ranch Prepack (FEI 1000519407), last inspected 2026-07-16 and classified VAI",
  "headline_cites": ["E15", "E16", "E14", "E12"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list records propranolol hydrochloride injection from Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC and Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. as Current with initial posting 2023-10-31 and updates through 2026-10-15.",
      "cites": ["E15", "E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our 40 mg tablets at both Corvale sites carry NDC 71335236909 labeled by Bryant Ranch Prepack, which operates FEI 1000519407 as a registered relabel/repack plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2026-07-16 and classified the inspection VAI, with the classification letter dated 2026-10-14.",
      "cites": ["E12", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier inspections at the same plant include an OAI classification in 2009 and multiple VAI classifications from 2010 through 2024.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6", "E7", "E8", "E9", "E10", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the plant on 2010-04-08.",
      "cites": ["E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage has remained on FDA's list for 36 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked option is to transfer 81 tablets of 40 mg from Corvale General (29.3 days on hand) to Corvale East (7.5 days on hand), which would bring Corvale East to 14 days while Corvale General retains two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D6"]
    }
  ]
}
